From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:16:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/52] MIPS: ingenic: Add SMP support for the X2600

The X2600 has two XBurst2 cores. Its core control unit (CCU) holds the
second one in reset and sets the address it starts from, and has a
mailbox per core whose interrupt, CPU interrupt line 3, serves as the
inter-processor interrupt. It also enables, per core, the interrupt lines
of the SoC interrupt controller, of the OST and of the mailboxes.

Add SMP operations for it: start a core at a small entry stub that
caches KSEG0 and loads the core's stack, raise IPIs through the
mailboxes, and let a secondary core take its mailbox and its own OST
timer. Peripheral interrupts stay with the boot CPU.

XBurst2 is weakly ordered, also around LL/SC, as Ingenic's own kernels
declare: select WEAK_ORDERING and WEAK_REORDERING_BEYOND_LLSC, without
which the SMP memory barriers are compiled out.

The register layout follows Ingenic's X2600 SDK kernel.
